        "answer": "RFC 9111: The no-store response directive indicates that a cache MUST NOT store any part of either the immediate request or the response and MUST NOT use the response to satisfy any other request. [S1](<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111.html>)\nRFC 9111: This directive applies to both private and shared caches. [S1](<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111.html>)\nRFC 9111: When a cache that implements the must-understand directive receives a response that includes it, the cache SHOULD ignore the no-store directive if it understands and implements the status code's caching requirements. [S1](<https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111.html>)",
